NG\\\\r\\\\nFigure 3.9.3.3\\\\r\\\\nCHAIN WIRE OR MESH FENCE\\\\r\\\\nNote: Fencing material with an aperture more than 13 mm, but less than 100 mm.\\\\r\\\\n21,404\\\\r\\\\nClause 3.9.3.2\\\\r\\\\nSUPERSEDED SUPERSEDED\\\",\\\"section\\\":null,\\\"score\\\":1,\\\"originalUrl\\\":\\\"/api/standards-library?document=82243ecea0760d56368c3ee94741bf47c53ca7eb37a37e4e09dfbc69f5aaad78#page=350\\\"},{\\\"id\\\":\\\"library:768aecc777a252ae8aea7debaebdb0c194faf7dab94420b164422ec4d412d823:350\\\",\\\"documentId\\\":\\\"768aecc777a252ae8aea7debaebdb0c194faf7dab94420b164422ec4d412d823\\\",\\\"documentName\\\":\\\"BCA_96_Volume_Two_Amdt_01_0.pdf\\\",\\\"edition\\\":\\\"Edition not established\\\",\\\"sha256\\\":\\\"768aecc777a252ae8aea7debaebdb0c194faf7dab94420b164422ec4d412d823\\\",\\\"page\\\":350,\\\"text\\\":\\\"21,404 PART \\\\r\\\\n⎯\\\\r\\\\n3.9.3.2 \\\\r\\\\n3.9.3.3 \\\\r\\\\nNote: l . \\\\r\\\\n3.9 - SAFE MOVEMENT AND ACCESS \\\\r\\\\nBuilding Code of Australia 1996 Volume Two \\\\r\\\\nFigure \\\\r\\\\nSPACING OF ACCESSIBLE HORIZONTAL MEMBERS, PROJECTIONS OR \\\\r\\\\nINDENTATIONS IN FENCING \\\\r\\\\nFigure \\\\r\\\\nCHAIN WIRE OR MESH FENCE \\\\r\\\\nFencing material with an aperture more than 13 mm, but ess than 100 mm\\\\r\\\\nClause 3.9.3.2 \\\\r\\\\nSUPERSEDED SUPERSEDED\\\",\\\"section\\\":null,\\\"score\\\":1,\\\"originalUrl\\\":\\\"/api/standards-library?document=768aecc777a252ae8aea7debaebdb0c194faf7dab94420b164422ec4d412d823#page=350\\\"}],\\\"scope\\\":\\\"Source excerpts only. Verify printed title, edition, jurisdiction and applicability before relying on a reference.\\\"}\"},{\"kind\":\"assistant\",\"tool\":null,\"failed\":null,\"origin\":null,\"projectName\":null,\"projectRevision\":null,\"text\":\"The local NCC library only carries building-code excerpts about pool/barrier fencing apertures; it does not hold the chain-wire product standard itself. I do not have a live web browser in this session, and I will not invent a designation, year or URL.\\n\\nHere is what I can confirm from the evidence I actually retrieved.\\n\\n## What the local standards library returned\\n\\nThe only on-device references that match \\\"chain wire mesh aperture\\\" are Building Code of Australia (BCA / NCC) Volume Two clauses on pool-safety barrier fencing — not the product standard for chain-wire mesh. Every excerpt carries the same Figure caption:\\n\\n- Source (retrieved now): on-device BCA/NCC PDF, search_standards_library topic \\\"chain wire fencing mesh aperture\\\".\\n- The note reads: \\\"Fencing material with an aperture more than 13 mm, but less than 100 mm\\\" (Figure 3.9.3.3, \\\"Chain wire or mesh fence\\\").\\n\\nRetrieved page URLs (all carry the watermark \\\"SUPERSEDED SUPERSEDED\\\" and are BCA 1996 amendments or BCA 2004–2009 Volume Two):\\n\\n- BCA 1996 Volume Two Amendment 0, p. 340 — sha256 a5574327…b6c4e\\n- BCA 1996 Volume Two Amendment 1, p. 350 — sha256 768aecc7…d823\\n- BCA 1996 Volume Two Amendment 2, p. 349 — sha256 550edb58…b842\\n- BCA 1996 Volume Two Amendment 3, p. 348 — sha256 81fcca6a…c657\\n- BCA 1996 Volume Two Amendment 4, p. 350 — sha256 82243ece…ad78\\n- BCA 1996 Volume Two Amendment 8, p. 330 — sha256 4bc1282e…e486\\n- BCA 1996 Volume Two Amendment 9, p. 331 — sha256 7ba564ab…a7d5\\n- BCA 1996 Volume Two Amendment 10, p. 333 — sha256 09f79d8c…f612\\n- BCA 1996 Volume Two Amendment 11, p. 337 — sha256 9d2df65b…19fa\\n- BCA 1996 Volume Two Amendment 12, p. 356 — sha256 f0059cd4…d5ce7\\n- BCA 1996 Volume Two Amendment 13, p. 358 — sha256 48bff03b…ca2e95\\n- BCA 2004 Volume Two, p. 380 — sha256 6b2f569f…fe68e (edition 2004)\\n- BCA 2005 Volume Two, p. 400 — sha256 70f824e2…cd32df (edition 2005)\\n- BCA 2006 Volume Two, p. 384 — sha256 94ac7293…24219 (edition 2006)\\n- BCA 2007 Volume Two, p. 394 — sha256 3003617f…b3e0f7 (edition 2007)\\n- BCA 2008 Volume Two, p. 391 — sha256 e3e49329…4e5976 (edition 2008)\\n- BCA 2009 Volume Two, p. 403 — sha256 a2133fa4…b6c4e (edition 2009)\\n\\nThese are BCA/NCC excerpts about pool-safety barrier geometry. They mention chain-wire mesh only as a fencing material that satisfies a 13–100 mm aperture rule. None of them is the product Standard that specifies chain-wire mesh aperture.\\n\\n## What I could not retrieve\\n\\nThe product Standard that actually specifies chain-wire (chain-link) fencing mesh aperture is published by Standards Australia. In this session I do not have a web-search tool available; I only have the on-device NCC/housing library, which does not index Standards Australia's chain-wire fencing standard. The Standards Australia catalogue (and SAI Global) is the only place I would cite a live \\\"AS …\\\" designation and current edition from, and I have no verified access to it right now.\\n\\nI will not invent a designation, year or URL. If you can either:\\n\\n- confirm a web-search tool is exposed for this session (none is in my current tool list), or\\n- paste the relevant Standards Australia / SAI Global page text,\\n\\nI will validate the designation, year and source URL against that evidence and cite only what is retrieved.\\n\\n## Honest limits to flag\\n\\n- Carried work-packet notes (the two prior checkpoints) recorded the same \\\"search failed\\\" outcome. I am not relying on them as a current tool receipt; I am reporting the same limitation again from this turn's own search.\\n- The BCA/NCC excerpts above all carry the watermark \\\"SUPERSEDED SUPERSEDED\\\". They are not the current NCC and they are not the product Standard; they are only evidence that the figure caption exists in older editions.\\n- Sample-data firewall kept: no sample, inferred or memory-only standard number has been promoted to a verified answer.\\n\\nIf you would like, I can broaden the on-device search to other terms (e.g. \\\"AS 2423\\\", \\\"chain link\\\", \\\"woven wire\\\", \\\"cyclone fence\\\") to see whether Standards Australia extracts are present locally, but the most likely honest result is the same: the chain-wire product Standard is not on this device.\\n\\nDeveloper review\\n- Outcome: Did not fabricate an answer; reported only retrieved BCA/NCC excerpts and named the unavailable web source.\\n- Friction: No web-search tool is exposed, so the exact AS designation, year and official URL cannot be produced this turn.\\n- Improvement: Add a Standards Australia / SAI Global web-fetch tool, or accept a pasted catalogue page to validate the designation.\"}],\"projectId\":\"job-da2d2767-cea0-4c2d-8b4d-3d9d5f349256\",\"activeId\":\"5f9dac7a-95f1-445a-b70e-23e88189fb91\",\"threads\":4,\"busy\":false,\"error\":null,\"workPacket\":{\"state\":\"review-required\",\"objective\":\"Search the web now for the current Australian Standard that specifies chain wire fencing mesh aperture, and give me its exact designation, its year of publication and the official source URL you retrieved it from. Cite the sources you actually retrieved.\",\"nextAction\":\"Workflow receipts complete. Review the draft against its sources and acceptance tests; no professional approval or issue recorded.\",\"pendingAction\":null,\"routingFailure\":null},\"entries\":[{\"kind\":\"user\",\"tool\":null,\"failed\":null,\"origin\":null,\"projectName\":null,\"projectRevision\":null,\"text\":\"Search the web now for the current Australian Standard that specifies chain wire fencing mesh aperture, and give me its exact designation, its year of publication and the official source URL you retrieved it from. Cite the sources you actually retrieved.\"},{\"kind\":\"assistant\",\"tool\":null,\"failed\":null,\"origin\":null,\"projectName\":null,\"projectRevision\":null,\"text\":\"I will set up the right workflow, then attempt the available local standards search and be clear about what I can and cannot retrieve.\\n\\n\"},{\"kind\":\"tool\",\"tool\":\"read_workflow_route\",\"failed\":null,\"origin\":\"model\",\"projectName\":\"New project\",\"projectRevision\":1,\"text\":\"{\\\"version\\\":\\\"xray.workflow/1\\\",\\\"workflow\\\":\\